{
  "note": "WIST-1 \u00a75.2 historical verification, ordinary case, over key identifiers alone: `declarations` carry seq, sealing height and keys; each Catalog carries its sealing height and signer. `expected.key_set_at` is the Key Set resolved at each height present, `verifies` and `rejected` (WIST1-E02) the Catalogs by that resolution. The recovery exception is exercised by catalog-recovery.json.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "rotation retiring the old key",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "label": "genesis",
          "seq": 0,
          "height": 1,
          "keys": [
            "k1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "rotation",
          "seq": 1,
          "height": 5,
          "keys": [
            "k2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "catalogs": [
        {
          "catalog_id": "c-below",
          "height": 4,
          "signer": "k1"
        },
        {
          "catalog_id": "c-beside-old",
          "height": 5,
          "signer": "k1"
        },
        {
          "catalog_id": "c-beside-new",
          "height": 5,
          "signer": "k2"
        },
        {
          "catalog_id": "c-above-old",
          "height": 6,
          "signer": "k1"
        },
        {
          "catalog_id": "c-above-new",
          "height": 6,
          "signer": "k2"
        }
      ],
      "expected": {
        "key_set_at": [
          {
            "height": 1,
            "keys": [
              "k1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "height": 4,
            "keys": [
              "k1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "height": 5,
            "keys": [
              "k2"
            ]
          },
          {
            "height": 6,
            "keys": [
              "k2"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "verifies": [
          "c-below",
          "c-beside-new",
          "c-above-new"
        ],
        "rejected": [
          "c-beside-old",
          "c-above-old"
        ]
      },
      "why": "\u00a75.2: the Key Set at height N is the highest-seq Declaration sealed at or below N, so a Catalog signed by the retired key verifies below the rotation's Epoch and nowhere at or above it \u2014 the Epoch's own Declaration applies first (WIST-3 \u00a73.3) \u2014 while the new key verifies from that Epoch onward."
    },
    {
      "name": "rotation keeping the old key",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "label": "genesis",
          "seq": 0,
          "height": 1,
          "keys": [
            "k1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "rotation",
          "seq": 1,
          "height": 5,
          "keys": [
            "k1",
            "k2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "catalogs": [
        {
          "catalog_id": "c-beside-old",
          "height": 5,
          "signer": "k1"
        },
        {
          "catalog_id": "c-above-old",
          "height": 9,
          "signer": "k1"
        }
      ],
      "expected": {
        "key_set_at": [
          {
            "height": 1,
            "keys": [
              "k1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "height": 5,
            "keys": [
              "k1",
              "k2"
            ]
          },
          {
            "height": 9,
            "keys": [
              "k1",
              "k2"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "verifies": [
          "c-beside-old",
          "c-above-old"
        ],
        "rejected": []
      },
      "why": "\u00a75.2: a rotation that carries the old key forward retires nothing, and Catalogs under it verify at every height."
    },
    {
      "name": "before the first declaration",
      "declarations": [
        {
          "label": "genesis",
          "seq": 0,
          "height": 1,
          "keys": [
            "k1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "label": "rotation",
          "seq": 1,
          "height": 5,
          "keys": [
            "k2"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "catalogs": [
        {
          "catalog_id": "c-orphan",
          "height": 0,
          "signer": "k1"
        }
      ],
      "expected": {
        "key_set_at": [
          {
            "height": 0,
            "keys": []
          },
          {
            "height": 1,
            "keys": [
              "k1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "height": 5,
            "keys": [
              "k2"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "verifies": [],
        "rejected": [
          "c-orphan"
        ]
      },
      "why": "\u00a75.2, WIST-3 \u00a73.3: no Declaration is sealed at or below the Catalog's height, so no Key Set applies and the Catalog does not verify \u2014 the Declaration must seal before or beside the first Catalog it authorizes."
    }
  ]
}
